    "blind_description": "This is a black-and-white line sketch showing a two-faced corner view of a building.\n\nVisible elements:\n- A gabled building corner is fully outlined, with two adjacent walls meeting at a front corner.\n- At the corner is a narrow, vertically outlined double door; a small vertical door handle line is visible, but the door’s full interior/open side is not drawn.\n- Each wall contains one large rectangular window with an inner frame and simple grid lines: a horizontal and two vertical lines make six pane sections; all pane divisions are complete.\n- Above both doors/windows, a rectangular projecting awning wraps the corner. Its outer box outline is complete; its lower edge has a repeated wavy scalloped valance, with short vertical segmenting lines above the waves.\n- Above the awning, two rectangular signs wrap the corner, one on each face. Each sign contains the clearly legible hand-drawn text “CAFE”.\n- The ground plane is indicated with a horizontal bottom edge and receding perspective lines.\n- In the foreground, there are three separate furniture fragments:\n  - On the left, one simple outlined chair, complete in basic outline.\n  - Center and right, two pedestal tables: each has a flat elongated tabletop, a single central stem, and a small diamond-shaped base. Their outlines are complete.\n- The building rear, roof undersides, additional walls, and any furniture beyond these three objects are not visible or missing. No people, textures, or shading are present.",
